"diploma","diploma","dee-PLOH-mah"],["seminar","seminar","say-mee-NAR"],["entrance exam","toelatingsexamen","TOO-lah-tings-ek-SAH-muhn"],["application","aanmelding","AHN-mel-ding"],["student card","studentenkaart","stoo-DEN-tuhn-kart"],["faculty","faculteit","fah-kul-TAYT"]]},{"id":"school-verbs","title":"School verbs","items":[["to study","studeren","stoo-DAY-ruhn"],["to teach","lesgeven","LES-khay-vuhn"],["to ask","vragen","VRAH-khuhn"],["to answer","antwoorden","ANT-vohr-duhn"],["to repeat","herhalen","hur-HAH-luhn"],["to understand","begrijpen","buh-KHRAY-puhn"],["to remember","onthouden","ont-HOW-duhn"],["to forget","vergeten","vuhr-KHAY-tuhn"],["to explain","uitleggen","OWT-lekh-uhn"],["to practise","oefenen","OO-fuh-nuhn"],["to pass an exam","slagen voor een examen","SLAH-khuhn vohr uhn ek-SAH-muhn"],["to fail an exam","zakken voor een examen","ZAK-uhn vohr uhn ek-SAH-muhn"],["to write down","opschrijven","OP-skhray-vuhn"],["to listen","luisteren","LOW-stuh-ruhn"],["to read aloud","hardop lezen","HART-op LAY-zuhn"],["to think","denken","DENG-kuhn"],["to count","tellen","TEL-uhn"],["to spell","spellen","SPEL-uhn"],["to translate","vertalen","vuhr-TAH-luhn"],["to graduate","afstuderen","AF-stoo-day-ruhn"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Dutch always uses the pronoun. \"Je\" is informal and \"u\" is formal. \"Hij\" is he, \"zij\" or \"ze\" is she, \"het\" is it."],"rows":[["I","ik","ik"],["you (informal)","jij / je","yay / yuh"],["he / she / it","hij / zij / het","hay / zay / uht"],["we","wij / we","vay / vuh"],["you (formal or plural)","u / jullie","oo / YUL-ee"],["they","zij / ze","zay / zuh"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ik ben student","ik ben stoo-DENT"],["you are tall","je bent lang","yuh bent lang"],["she is my older sister","zij is mijn oudere zus","zay is mayn OW-duh-ruh zus"],["we are friends","wij zijn vrienden","vay zayn VREEN-duhn"],["they are teachers","zij zijn leraren","zay zayn LAY-rah-ruhn"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Most nouns add -en or -s: boek, boeken. Some change a letter: huis, huizen. After a number the plural is used: twee boeken."],"rows":[["boek (book)","boeken","BOO-kuhn"],["huis (house)","huizen","HOW-zuhn"],["kind (child)","kinderen","KIN-duh-ruhn"],["tafel (table)","tafels","TAH-fuhls"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","één huis, huizen","ayn hows HOW-zuhn"],["one book, books","één boek, boeken","ayn book BOO-kuhn"],["one cat, cats","één kat, katten","ayn kat KAT-uhn"],["two books","twee boeken","tvay BOO-kuhn"],["the children","de kinderen","duh KIN-duh-ruhn"]]},{"id":"to-be-zijn","title":"To be: zijn","text":["\"Zijn\" (to be) is irregular. Learn all the forms."],"rows":[["I am","ik ben","ik ben"],["you are","je bent","yuh bent"],["he / she is","hij is","hay is"],["we are","wij zijn","vay zayn"],["you are (formal)","u bent","oo bent"],["they are","zij zijn","zay zayn"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ik ben student","ik ben stoo-DENT"],["you are tired","je bent moe","yuh bent moo"],["he is a doctor","hij is dokter","hay is DOK-tuhr"],["we are happy","wij zijn blij","vay zayn blay"],["they are at home","zij zijn thuis","zay zayn tows"]]},{"id":"hebben-have","title":"Hebben: have","text":["\"Hebben\" (to have): ik heb, jij hebt, hij heeft, wij hebben. \"Er is\" means \"there is\"."],"rows":[["I have","ik heb","ik hep"],["you have","je hebt","yuh hept"],["he / she has","hij heeft","hay hayft"],["we have","wij hebben","vay HEB-uhn"],["you have (formal)","u hebt","oo hept"],["they have","zij hebben","zay HEB-uhn"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","ik heb een oudere broer","ik hep uhn OW-duh-ruh broor"],["I have a car","ik heb een auto","ik hep uhn OW-toh"],["I do not have time","ik heb geen tijd","ik hep khayn tayt"],["there is a problem","er is een probleem","er is uhn proh-BLAYM"],["there is no water","er is geen water","er is khayn VAH-tuhr"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense","text":["Take the stem (werken, werk-) and add: -, -t, -t, -en. Werken (to work): ik werk, jij werkt, hij werkt, wij werken."],"rows":[["I work","ik werk","ik verk"],["you work","je werkt","yuh verkt"],["he / she works","hij werkt","hay verkt"],["we work","wij werken","vay VER-kuhn"],["you work (formal)","u werkt","oo verkt"],["they work","zij werken","zay VER-kuhn"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","ik eet brood","ik ayt broht"],["you are reading a book","je leest een boek","yuh layst uhn book"],["she works in a bank","zij werkt bij een bank","zay verkt bay uhn bank"],["we drink tea","wij drinken thee","vay DRING-kuhn tay"],["they are sleeping","zij slapen","zay SLAH-puhn"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb is always the second item: Ik lees een boek. If another word comes first, the verb still stays second: Vandaag lees ik een boek."],"rows":[["I read a book","ik lees een boek","ik lays uhn book"],["she drinks tea","zij drinkt thee","zay drinkt tay"],["we go to school","wij gaan naar school","vay khahn nahr skhohl"]],"ex":[["I read a book","ik lees een boek","ik lays uhn book"],["he drinks tea","hij drinkt thee","hay drinkt tay"],["we go to school","wij gaan naar school","vay khahn nahr skhohl"],["they eat bread","zij eten brood","zay AY-tuhn broht"],["the teacher writes","de leraar schrijft","duh LAY-rahr skhrayft"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Use \"niet\" for verbs and adjectives, and \"geen\" for nouns with \"een\": Ik heb geen auto."],"rows":[["I go","ik ga","ik khah"],["I do not go","ik ga niet","ik khah neet"],["is","is","is"],["is not","is niet","is neet"]],"ex":[["I want","ik wil","ik vil"],["I do not want","ik wil niet","ik vil neet"],["I speak English","ik spreek Engels","ik sprayk ENG-uhls"],["I do not speak English","ik spreek geen Engels","ik sprayk khayn ENG-uhls"],["I like it","ik vind het leuk","ik vint uht luhk"],["I do not like it","ik vind het niet leuk","ik vint uht neet luhk"],["she is here","zij is hier","zay is heer"],["she is not here","zij is hier niet","zay is heer neet"],["I have a car","ik heb een auto","ik hep uhn OW-toh"],["I do not have a car","ik heb geen auto","ik hep khayn OW-toh"],["I understand","ik begrijp het","ik buh-KHRAYP uht"],["I do not understand","ik begrijp het niet","ik buh-KHRAYP uht neet"],["we are tired","wij zijn moe","vay zayn moo"],["we are not tired","wij zijn niet moe","vay zayn neet moo"],["he works on Sundays","hij werkt op zondag","hay verkt op ZON-dakh"],["he does not work on Sundays","hij werkt niet op zondag","hay verkt neet op ZON-dakh"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Put the verb first: Ben je student? A question word goes before the verb: Waar woon je?"],"rows":[["you are a student","je bent student","yuh bent stoo-DENT"],["are you a student?","ben je student?","ben yuh stoo-DENT"],["he is here","hij is hier","hay is heer"],["is he here?","is hij hier?","is hay heer"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","is dit jouw boek?","is dit yow book"],["are they here?","zijn zij hier?","zayn zay heer"],["do you like tea?","hou je van thee?","how yuh van tay"],["is it cold?","is het koud?","is uht kowt"],["do you speak English?","spreekt u Engels?","spraykt oo ENG-uhls"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["A question word comes first, then the verb."],"rows":[["what","wat","vat"],["who","wie","vee"],["where","waar","vahr"],["when","wanneer","va-NAYR"],["why","waarom","vahr-OM"],["how","hoe","hoo"],["how much","hoeveel","hoo-VAYL"],["which","welk","velk"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","hoe heet je?","hoo hayt yuh"],["who is he?","wie is hij?","vee is hay"],["where do you live?","waar woon je?","vahr vohn yuh"],["when is the lesson?","wanneer is de les?","va-NAYR is duh les"],["why are you late?","waarom ben je te laat?","vahr-OM ben yuh tuh laht"],["how much is it?","hoeveel kost het?","hoo-VAYL kost uht"],["which book?","welk boek?","velk book"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Put the word before the noun: mijn (my), jouw / je (your), zijn (his), haar (her), ons or onze (our), uw (your, formal), hun (their). To like something, use \"leuk vinden\" or \"houden van\"."],"rows":[["my book","mijn boek","mayn book"],["your book","jouw boek","yow book"],["his / her book","zijn boek / haar boek","zayn book / hahr book"],["our book","ons boek","ons book"],["your book (formal)","uw boek","oo book"]],"ex":[["my phone","mijn telefoon","mayn tay-luh-FOHN"],["your house (formal)","uw huis","oo hows"],["his sister","zijn zus","zayn zus"],["I like music","ik hou van muziek","ik how van moo-ZEEK"],["I love football","ik ben dol op voetbal","ik ben dol op VOOT-bal"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["jij / je (informal): friends, family, children. u (formal): strangers, older people, work. The verb changes only a little: je hebt, u hebt."],"rows":[["how are you?","hoe gaat het met je? / met u?","hoo khaht uht met yuh / met oo"],["you speak","je spreekt / u spreekt","yuh spraykt / oo spraykt"],["your name","je naam / uw naam","yuh nahm / oo nahm"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","hoe gaat het met je?","hoo khaht uht met yuh"],["how are you? (formal)","hoe gaat het met u?","hoo khaht uht met oo"],["where are you going? (informal)","waar ga je heen?","vahr khah yuh hayn"],["where are you going? (formal)","waar gaat u heen?","vahr khaht oo hayn"],["please sit down (formal)","gaat u zitten, alstublieft","khaht oo ZIT-uhn, ahl-stoo-BLEEFT"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: the perfect tense, \"hebben\" or \"zijn\" + ge-...-d / -t. Ik heb gewerkt (I worked). Future: \"gaan\" + verb, or just the present with a time word."],"rows":[["I went","ik ben gegaan","ik ben khuh-KHAHN"],["you went","je bent gegaan","yuh bent khuh-KHAHN"],["he went","hij is gegaan","hay is khuh-KHAHN"],["we went","wij zijn gegaan","vay zayn khuh-KHAHN"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","gisteren was ik moe","KHIS-tuh-ruhn vas ik moo"],["I will study tomorrow","morgen ga ik studeren","MOR-khuhn khah ik stoo-DAY-ruhn"],["we went to the park","wij zijn naar het park gegaan","vay zayn nahr uht park khuh-KHAHN"],["I saw him","ik heb hem gezien","ik hep hem khuh-ZEEN"],["she wrote a letter","zij heeft een brief geschreven","zay hayft uhn breef khuh-SKHRAY-vuhn"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal: the verb stem (kom). Formal: stem + t, with \"u\" (komt u). To forbid, use \"niet\" or \"geen\"."],"rows":[["come (informal)","kom","kom"],["come (formal)","komt u","komt oo"],["do not come","kom niet","kom neet"],["sit down","ga zitten","khah ZIT-uhn"]],"ex":[["come here","kom hier","kom heer"],["do not come here","kom hier niet","kom heer neet"],["sit down","ga zitten","khah ZIT-uhn"],["do not sit down","ga niet zitten","khah neet ZIT-uhn"],["be quiet","wees stil","vays stil"],["do not be late","kom niet te laat","kom neet tuh laht"],["open the door","open de deur","OH-puhn duh duhr"],["close the window","sluit het raam","slowt uht rahm"],["listen to me","luister naar mij","LOW-stuhr nahr may"],["do not worry","maak je geen zorgen","mahk yuh khayn ZOR-khuhn"],["speak slowly","spreek langzaam","sprayk LANG-zahm"],["wait a moment","wacht even","vakht AY-vuhn"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Kunnen (can): ik kan. Moeten (must): ik moet. Willen (want): ik wil. The second verb goes to the end, in its basic form."],"rows":[["I can swim","ik kan zwemmen","ik kan ZVEM-uhn"],["I cannot swim","ik kan niet zwemmen","ik kan neet ZVEM-uhn"],["I must go","ik moet gaan","ik moot khahn"],["I want to go","ik wil gaan","ik vil khahn"]],"ex":[["I can swim","ik kan zwemmen","ik kan ZVEM-uhn"],["I cannot swim","ik kan niet zwemmen","ik kan neet ZVEM-uhn"],["can you help me?","kunt u mij helpen?","kunt oo may HEL-puhn"],["we must go","wij moeten gaan","vay MOO-tuhn khahn"],["we must not go","wij mogen niet gaan","vay MOH-khuhn neet khahn"],["I want to eat","ik wil eten","ik vil AY-tuhn"],["I do not want to eat","ik wil niet eten","ik vil neet AY-tuhn"],["you can come","je kunt komen","yuh kunt KOH-muhn"],["you cannot come","je kunt niet komen","yuh kunt neet KOH-muhn"],["she wants to study","zij wil studeren","zay vil stoo-DAY-ruhn"],["I must work today","ik moet vandaag werken","ik moot van-DAHKH VER-kuhn"],["you must not run","je mag niet rennen","yuh makh neet REN-uhn"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Common words: in (in), op (on), bij (at, near), naar (to), van (from, of), met (with), onder (under)."],"rows":[["in","in","in"],["on","op","op"],["at / near","bij","bay"],["to","naar","nahr"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","het boek ligt op de tafel","uht book likht op duh TAH-fuhl"],["the cat is under the table","de kat zit onder de tafel","duh kat zit ON-duhr duh TAH-fuhl"],["I am at school","ik ben op school","ik ben op skhohl"],["I am at home","ik ben thuis","ik ben tows"],["the shop is next to the bank","de winkel is naast de bank","duh VING-kuhl is nahst duh bank"],["the park is near the station","het park is bij het station","uht park is bay uht stah-SHON"],["we meet in the morning","wij ontmoeten elkaar 's ochtends","vay ont-MOO-tuhn el-KAHR SOKH-tuhnts"],["the lesson is at nine","de les is om negen uur","duh les is om NAY-khuhn oor"],["the key is in the bag","de sleutel zit in de tas","duh SLUH-tuhl zit in duh tas"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -er for \"more\": groot, groter. For \"the most\" add -st: groot, grootst (het grootste). \"Than\" is \"dan\". Irregular: goed, beter, best."],"rows":[["big, bigger, the biggest","groot, groter, het grootst","khroht, KHROH-tuhr, uht khrohtst"],["small, smaller, the smallest","klein, kleiner, het kleinst","klayn, KLAY-nuhr, uht klaynst"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","groot, groter, het grootst","khroht KHROH-tuhr uht khrohtst"],["small, smaller, the smallest","klein, kleiner, het kleinst","klayn KLAY-nuhr 